{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets","id":214099,"title":"Cold Iron Bullets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-30T17:45:47-07:00","id":214099,"title":"Cold Iron Bullets","content":"Not sure if this should go into Changeling or Hunter, but are there rules for Cold Iron bullets anywhere? I could swear there are, but I can't find them.<br /> <br /> Me and some friends are currently having a disagreement about whether Cold Iron can be fired from a gun and still be called Cold Iron. The argument is that because gunpowder is a manmade fire, it turns Cold Iron into just Iron. I disagree, but I'm looking for rules that say otherwise. And also my Hunter might need some Cold Iron bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T18:20:14-07:00","id":214145,"title":"","content":"Rites of Spring carries the entire discussion on Cold Iron.<br /> <br /> I'd argue for simplicity's sake that firing a cold iron bullet does not screw with it to the point of losing it's metaphysical properties. The reasons for this are two. One, making cold iron bullets without heating it takes a shit ton of work, and it's not something most players will do. Two, bullets generally aren't retrievable, and as such using cold iron for bullets is wasting resources. In short, it's a troublesome weapon-no need to make it worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T18:24:31-07:00","id":214149,"title":"","content":"Cold Iron, in Changeling, is just relatively pure iron. It being heated would have no effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T18:27:53-07:00","id":214151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets?p=214149#post214149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold Iron, in Changeling, is just relatively pure iron. It being heated would have no effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the metaphysics the ST puts into effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T18:28:07-07:00","id":214152,"title":"","content":"Unless you're thinking of Hand-Forged Iron, in which case, yeah, I'd agree with Arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T18:31:06-07:00","id":214155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets?p=214151#post214151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the metaphysics the ST puts into effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose? Because Rites of Spring sets it out pretty clearly. <br /> <br /> &quot;As stated in Changeling the Lost, 'Cold Iron' is defined as Iron that is 'relatively pure'&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T18:33:06-07:00","id":214175,"title":"","content":"Edit: Double Post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":276,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","user":"Merkonan","date":". 07-30-2014, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T06:18:17-07:00","id":214586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets?p=214145#post214145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites of Spring carries the entire discussion on Cold Iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites of Spring is actually what started all this. Because &quot;The Foe of All Unreason&quot; claims that fire is magic, and says that putting manmade flame to Cold Iron turns it away from Cold Iron, that the flame from gunpowder counts as manmade flame.<br /> That just seems incredibly ridiculous to me, though, as it's not as if the flame is being intentionally introduced to the bullet to make it better in any way. Or even being put to it longer than a split second.<br /> <br /> That's why I was wondering if there are any actual rules for making Cold Iron bullets. It would show once and for all that Cold Iron can be fired from a gun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:40:14-07:00","id":214653,"title":"","content":"I spent a year running Changeling and I still get confused on this subject. So, bearing that in mind... isn't Cold Iron the one with the incredibly misleading name? Cold Iron can be heated and forged, it just has to mostly be unrefined iron. So, as long as you find a way to manufacture iron bullets, you can probably make bullets that break through fae defences.<br /> <br /> Which leaves Hand-forged Iron, the cause of aggravated damage to the Fae, as the one that can't be introduced to flame. And, well, a hand-forged bullet seems like it would be pretty hard to pull off in a way that wouldn't see a modern gun jam. I seem to remember that I pretty much ruled it was impossible for my group, although I do recall debate over whether it would be possible to do with a blunderbuss. Can't remember if we came to a verdict on that one, no one really wanted to go to the effort of getting a blunderbuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T01:04:42-07:00","id":215662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets?p=214586#post214586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites of Spring is actually what started all this. Because &quot;The Foe of All Unreason&quot; claims that fire is magic, and says that putting manmade flame to Cold Iron turns it away from Cold Iron, that the flame from gunpowder counts as manmade flame.<br /> That just seems incredibly ridiculous to me, though, as it's not as if the flame is being intentionally introduced to the bullet to make it better in any way. Or even being put to it longer than a split second.<br /> <br /> That's why I was wondering if there are any actual rules for making Cold Iron bullets. It would show once and for all that Cold Iron can be fired from a gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hand-Forged. It talks about putting manmade flame to Hand-Forged Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T16:24:04-07:00","id":217029,"title":"","content":"Sigh, this is the volcano discussion all over again.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron is one of the most aggravating concepts in changeling the lost.<br /> First, cold iron is pure Iron, minimal traces of other elements on the mix. <br /> Second, rites of spring brings in the &quot;flame caused by the hand of man&quot; idea, which I still think is dumb, because it creates a thousand and one exceptions, (solar forge, volcanic forge). Previously Iron that was physically cold was good enough, now people complicate it. <br /> <br /> If you use a home made gauss rifle it would count as cold iron, if you used a sling it would...silliness.<br /> <br /> The point of tempering and pounding iron is to pound out the impurities of the metal, there is no way the spark from gunpowder would be heating up the iron enough to smelt in the milliseconds the bullet exists in the barrel, now the problem is the effort to shape an iron bullet without using a cast mold","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T07:41:35-07:00","id":225960,"title":"","content":"It would be impossible for a human to hand-forge a bullet with enough precision to not jam, but I would probably allow a Smith or maybe an Inventor to do it. The whole &quot;putting man made flame [to iron]&quot; thing is meant to be poetic, I think. Just touching it with fire shouldn't be enough to break the magic, it's the process of tempering it to remove the natural impurities that does it. The purpose of the gunpowder is to propel the bullet, not to temper it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T23:16:09-07:00","id":243660,"title":"","content":"On the other hand you could probably bang a lump of iron into a ball in the fashion of a musket round. And you might even be able to get that round fired off from a shot gun. Then again, it'd be way easier just to fill up a shot gun with &quot;hand forged iron&quot; dust and use it as buckshot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T04:43:24-07:00","id":245276,"title":"","content":"I've seen shotguns take a lot of punishment, no doubt some models could take such abuse quite easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T23:30:04-07:00","id":255083,"title":"","content":"If the iron was the buckshot, then it could be filings, pellets, scrap...if it fits in the shell it will fire. Wont be good for the barrel, but thats up to the pc with the high crafts rating and the proper tools to deal with. As a ST, id simply put a limit on the amount of roinds that could be fired before the barrel is damaged (loss of damage and accuracy) and then another round or two before your barrel becomes slag and you need to take a trip to Gander Mt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T01:11:31-07:00","id":255112,"title":"","content":"One thing is sure - Cold Iron thing should be solved in 2ed of <b>Changling.</b> Also, would love to hear official answer from developers on this in topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T14:39:22-07:00","id":256836,"title":"","content":"According to the great &amp; all-knowing wiki, &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore#Cold_iron\" target=\"_blank\">Cold Iron</a>&quot; could refer to most ferrous compounds (including many <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel\" target=\"_blank\">steels</a>), while others seem to imply that the phrase refers to forms of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrought_iron\" target=\"_blank\">wrought iron</a> that were used to create various objects (including swords, cutlery, horseshoes, chains, and other objects) before the creation &amp; use of steel became commonplace.<br /> <br /> In theory, one could also fashion a slug of &quot;cold iron&quot; &amp; fit it into a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabot#Cup_sabot\" target=\"_blank\">cup-type sabot</a> (available from several commercial manufacturers) with the powder charge behind the sabot, such that the heated gases make no significant contact with the slug itself (if that is a concern).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images.cabelas.com/is/image/cabelas/s7_215461_999_01?rgn=0,0,342,483&amp;scl=1&amp;fmt=jpeg&amp;id=12xhqcZTpylySgQz6MAM3B\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Alternatively, one could also just use EM accelerators - e.g. railguns and/or coilguns. Though, that might be limited by one's access to the needed underlying technologies &amp; the anticipated armor (or lack thereof) of the target - <a href=\"http://www.popsci.com/technology/article/2013-08/watch-homemade-coilgun-destroy-laptop\" target=\"_blank\">this homemade coilgun</a>, as impressive as its destruction of a laptop computer may look, can only achieve a muzzle velocity of ~138 ft/s (~42 m/s), which is well below even the most modest of modern conventional firearms; one would arguably be better off fashioning 'cold iron&quot; arrow heads and buying a good compound bow (where 200+ ft/s is apparently common) if the goal is &quot;long-range anti-fae combat&quot;.<br /> <br /> How much of a game-mechanics advantage/bonus do &quot;cold steel&quot; weapons usually produce versus their non-&quot;cold steel&quot; counterparts in CtL?<br /> Is it really worth it to go through the trouble of producing such a thing as &quot;cold iron bullets&quot;, versus using larger-caliber conventional (or HE) rounds?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/212-stormbringer","name":"Stormbringer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T20:49:05-07:00","id":256970,"title":"","content":"Cold iron is to changlings as silver is to werewolves. Thats why even if the damage is lower, its technically more effective. I like the idea of a blunderbus or misket to fire cold iron musket balls. Feels extra changling to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T15:02:25-07:00","id":259273,"title":"","content":"And as a bonus, a musket might be less prone to jamming and breakage in the deep hedge than a modern firearm is. I like to think that the more ancient and less technical the machine or tool is, the further you can take it into the Fairy world before it starts to suffer issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T22:18:22-07:00","id":267210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets#post214099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me and some friends are currently having a disagreement about whether Cold Iron can be fired from a gun and still be called Cold Iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tales from the corebook-rereading!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL Core Rulebook, p41, &quot;Changeling Life - Acceptance and Membership&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally, these executions are carried out in the mortal world, using a cold (wrought) iron implement. These weapons range from rare and archaic choices, such as beheading the offender with an axe, to <b>the more common option of specially made wrought-iron bullets or shot.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T00:21:20-07:00","id":267249,"title":"","content":"In some ways iron is more dangerous to changelings than silver is to werewolves. Changelings may not take aggravated from it, but it bypasses most of the defenses and armor that a changeling is likely to possess.<br /> <br /> I generally follow the guidelines in <i>Rites of Spring</i>. Whether something is &quot;cold iron&quot; isn't about purity. Otherwise steel is more likely to qualify than cast iron, and iron ore wouldn't have a chance which just seems wrong, A substance is made out of &quot;cold iron&quot; if it is something that common sense says is iron--not steel or an oxide or an intentionally created alloy. Similarly, hand-forged iron follows a more fairytale interpretation than a scientific one. Iron is no longer hand-forged if the smith smelts it or shapes it with tools that don't rely on their own muscles. There's some arguments about whether or not certain things count as loopholes (volcanoes, etc), but I tend to apply the <i>Dresden Files'</i> &quot;Free Will&quot; logic to it. Was it smelted because of an act of will or is it something that just happened naturally? This basically limits hand-forged iron to iron ore (which hasn't been worked at all), meteoric iron (smelted by reentry instead of by a person), or by Wizened Smiths who spend a *dot* of Willpower to circumvent the smelting restrictions.<br /> <br /> The Mind's Eye Society has an addendum that iron bullets will no longer be hand-forged when fired out of a gun. That seems reasonable to me, although it's up to interpretation.<br /> <br /> ETA - The bullet would still be &quot;cold iron&quot; though, because, by <i>Rites of Spring</i> guidelines, the &quot;cold&quot; part of &quot;cold iron&quot; is just poetic, not a requirement. Basically, &quot;cold iron&quot; is pretty easy to acquire/craft. It's when you want a hand-forged weapon to take on a True Fae that things become difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 09-28-2014, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T06:33:00-07:00","id":287532,"title":"","content":"I think then a modern crossbow firing bolts with hand forged iron tips would be more sensible option than a firearm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T05:47:37-07:00","id":290456,"title":"","content":"This whole problem started back in Dungeons &amp; Dragons, where &quot;cold iron&quot; (a poetic reference not unlike &quot;hot lead&quot; killing a gangster) was somehow some kind of special iron not forged with heat, which is completely silly.<br /> <br /> In the initial release of Changeling, iron that worked to bypass defenses and cause aggravated damage to the True Fae was anything iron <i>forged by hand</i> - that is, not manufactured by an impersonal factory, but crafted by a craftsman. But then Rites of Spring revisited the rules and confused the issue, demanding some level of &quot;purity&quot; but allowing mass-manufactured goods.<br /> <br /> For sake of flavor, I like the hand-crafted requirement. An iron sword will work, as long as someone actually made it by hand, with care and attention. An iron bullet will work fine, as long as the gunsmith actually smelted the ore and cast the rounds himself.<br /> <br /> As for whether steel counts, I think in Changeling terms the &quot;steel&quot; and &quot;iron&quot; entities have a different set of contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T07:37:42-07:00","id":290484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/214099-cold-iron-bullets?p=290456#post290456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sake of flavor, I like the hand-crafted requirement. An iron sword will work, as long as someone actually made it by hand, with care and attention. An iron bullet will work fine, as long as the gunsmith actually smelted the ore and cast the rounds himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally now envision Hunter hand-crafting his iron bullets and being very angry on meeting with his Fae pray:&quot; I spent 5 deays on crafting this bullets clip for my gun, just to kill you. Now I wil, finally!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T04:05:23-07:00","id":291169,"title":"","content":"I would just play safe in his situation and snipe the shit out of Fae, if that would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T22:26:13-08:00","id":301834,"title":"","content":"Another point I like to bring up to my dear PCs:<br /> Guess what: If you want to use a cold iron weapon you're holding onto Glamour Kryptonite!<br /> No defenses, no powers, pretty much fucked for contracts.<br /> You can cut through defenses, but using it will cut through yours unless you get some mundane armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}